-- EXPERIMENT extraction-throughput query -- Sema translation of
-- query/flockmtl/Q103.sql, arm (a): QUESTION-FORM PROMPT.
--
-- Selected with SEMA_QUERY_VARIANT=question.
--
-- Semantically the same task as Q103.sql, reworded because Sema's semantic map
-- cannot reliably parse its own response under the verbatim flockmtl wording.
-- On a 3-row fixture this phrasing returned clean, correct answers on all rows
-- ("The sentiment of this review is POSITIVE.") where the verbatim prompt
-- returned empty strings. The reply is a full sentence rather than a bare
-- label, which the evaluator handles: _evaluate_q103's canon() substring-matches
-- POSITIVE / NEGATIVE.
--
-- THIS IS A DISCLOSED DEVIATION FROM PROMPT PARITY. It must be reported as such
-- alongside Q103.sql (the verbatim arm), not silently substituted for it: the
-- pair is what separates "Sema classifies badly" from "Sema fails to parse its
-- own output". Also disclose the structured-output difference -- Sema uses
-- JSON-object mode while the flock arms drive guided_json/xgrammar.
--
-- Column order matters: column 0 = reviewId, column 1 = predicted label.
SELECT
  reviewId,
  s'What is the sentiment of this review, POSITIVE or NEGATIVE? {reviewText}' AS predicted_sentiment
FROM reviews_2000;
